{"v":1,"st":"OH","y":"2022","L":{"cd":{"f":"2022-cd.json","n":15,"lbl":"U.S. House","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2022_us_cd118_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2022/shp/cb_2022_us_cd118_500k.zip","7d16875ca4d56f63402b122e37a47690a0b3edb30129b475b7d3e79191dcf774"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's lines of the 118th Congress's districts (its file says session 118).","chk":[15,15,0],"why":"","rec":["The 'March 2 plan': remedial congressional plan, 15 districts, adopted by the Ohio Redistricting Commission 2022-03-02","2022-05-03","Supreme Court of Ohio, Neiman v. LaRose, 2022-Ohio-2471 (decided 2022-07-19): the March 2 plan, the May 3 primary held under it","https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/0/2022/2022-Ohio-2471.pdf","It replaced the General Assembly's S.B. 258 plan (signed 2021-11-20), which the Ohio Supreme Court struck on 2022-01-14 (Adams v. DeWine). The May 3 primary was held under the March 2 plan. The Ohio Supreme Court struck this plan too on 2022-07-19, but no replacement was possible before November, and it was used on 2022-11-08 (that ruling was later vacated by the U.S. Supreme Court, and the case ended in 2023). The cd118 file has 15 districts and fits the 2022 returns at municipality level (99.5%); the cd116 file fits 65.9%."],"c":15,"lv":{"federal":15}},"sldu":{"f":"2022-sldu.json","n":33,"lbl":"State Senate","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2022_us_sldu_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2022/shp/cb_2022_us_sldu_500k.zip","a58879d76e18dd617823ed6725904933625bc34c5242061694557a6654681a8c"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's 2022 file of legislative districts, the lines it records for the 2022 legislative session year.","chk":[17,17,0],"why":"","rec":["'Map 3': the Ohio Redistricting Commission's third General Assembly plan, adopted 2022-02-24 (33 Senate districts)","2022-08-02","U.S. District Court, S.D. Ohio, Gonidakis v. LaRose, No. 2:22-cv-773, opinion of 2022-04-20: Map 3 to govern 2022 (copy at All About Redistricting)","https://redistricting.lls.edu/wp-content/uploads/OH-gonidakis-20220420-opinion-ordering-feb-24-map.pdf","Struck by the Ohio Supreme Court on 2022-03-16, but a federal three-judge court ordered Map 3 used for the 2022 elections only (opinion 2022-04-20, order 2022-05-27); the primary moved to 2022-08-02. Odd-numbered Senate districts were up (17 contests). The Census file's own metadata says its lines are the ones 'collected ... for the 2022 election year', i.e. Map 3, and the file's fit to the 2022 returns agrees (99.3% of matched votes in municipalities touching the district, against 93.2% for the 2024 file). The Census documents do not name Map 3, so the match is by that metadata plus the fit."],"c":17,"lv":{"legislature":17}},"sldl":{"f":"2022-sldl.json","n":99,"lbl":"State House","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2022_us_sldl_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2022/shp/cb_2022_us_sldl_500k.zip","2c53165336841eaefc0022fa07129605e5e337e307380a1275977f729d9b84d6"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's 2022 file of legislative districts, the lines it records for the 2022 legislative session year.","chk":[99,99,0],"why":"","rec":["'Map 3': the Ohio Redistricting Commission's third General Assembly plan, adopted 2022-02-24 (99 House districts)","2022-08-02","U.S. District Court, S.D. Ohio, Gonidakis v. LaRose, No. 2:22-cv-773, opinion of 2022-04-20: Map 3 to govern 2022 (copy at All About Redistricting)","https://redistricting.lls.edu/wp-content/uploads/OH-gonidakis-20220420-opinion-ordering-feb-24-map.pdf","As the Senate entry: ordered for 2022 only by the federal court after the Ohio Supreme Court struck it on 2022-03-16. The Census file's own metadata says its lines are the ones 'collected ... for the 2022 election year', i.e. Map 3, and the file's fit to the 2022 returns agrees (99.7% of matched votes in municipalities touching the district; 93.3% for the 2024 file; 35.8% for the 2020 